==Dutch==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|nl|dum|buurt||district}} (also {{m|dum|buyrte}}) [15th century], from {{m|dum|ghebuerte||surroundings}} [c. 1290] and {{m|dum|gebuerde||zone}} [c. 1240], related to {{cog|goh|giburida}}.<ref>{{R:nl:Etymologiebank|buurt}}</ref>  Akin to {{cog|fy|buert}}. See also
{{m|nl|gebied}} and Belgian Dutch synonym {{m|nl|gebuurte}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/byrt/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-buurt.ogg|audio}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|buurt}}
* {{rhymes|nl|yːrt}}

===Noun===
{{nl-noun|f|-en|buurtje}}

# [[neighborhood]], part of town.
#: ''Het ligt in de buurt van Groningen.'' - It is nearby Groningen.
# [[vicinity]], [[proximity]]
#: ''Hij is in de buurt.'' - He is close by.

